# The server image builds from the repository root, so this is what decides how much of the
# working tree gets sent to the daemon. Build outputs are the expensive part, and copying a
# host-built bin/ into the image would also silently override what the build stage produced.

**/bin/
**/obj/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/

.git/
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/
.agents/

# Nothing under here is an input to an image build, and the compose bundle is what consumes
# the images rather than the other way round.
deploy/
docs/
openapi/

**/*.md
!CLAUDE.md

FutureFlags.AppHost/
FutureFlags.Domain.Tests/
FutureFlags.Server.Tests/

**/.env
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
